0 -13 Td (Executive summary) Tj
0 -13 Td (These guidelines provide guidance on the application of Article 37 LED, in particular on the legal) Tj
0 -13 Td (standard for appropriate safeguards to be applied by competent authorities pursuant to Article) Tj
0 -13 Td (37\(1\)\(a\) and \(b\) LED and, accordingly, on the relevant factors for the assessment of whether such) Tj
0 -13 Td (safeguards exist. These guidelines therefore include an indication as to the EDPBs expectations of) Tj
0 -13 Td (Member States, as negotiating parties, when envisaging concluding or amending a legally binding) Tj
0 -13 Td (instrument between the concerned Member State\(s\) and a third country or international organisation) Tj
0 -13 Td (pursuant to Article 37\(1\)\(a\) LED.) Tj
0 -13 Td (The EDPB notes that Article 35\(3\) LED applies to transfers carried out under Article 37 LED. Article 37) Tj
0 -13 Td (LED should therefore be applied in light of the principle that the level of data protection applicable in) Tj
0 -13 Td (the European Union must not be undermined by the transfer of personal data to another jurisdiction.) Tj
0 -13 Td (The EDPB concludes that Article 37 LED requires an essentially equivalent level of data protection in) Tj
0 -13 Td (the recipient third country or international organisation. However, this requirement relates to the) Tj
0 -13 Td (specific data transfer or category of transfers at hand. Pursuant to Article 37 LED, essential equivalence) Tj
0 -13 Td (to the protection guaranteed under the LED should be ensured for that particular case and not) Tj
0 -13 Td (necessarily with regard to the entire existing legislation in the third country or international) Tj
0 -13 Td (organisation.) Tj
0 -13 Td (The EDPB has already adopted Recommendations on the adequacy referential under the LED,) Tj
0 -13 Td (addressing which data protection principles have to be present to ensure essential equivalence with) Tj
0 -13 Td (the EU framework within the scope of the LED. The EDPB considers that the principles and safeguards) Tj
0 -13 Td (outlined in these Recommendations apply in substance in the context of Article 37 LED, i.e. with regard) Tj
0 -13 Td (to the specific transfer or category of transfers.) Tj
0 -13 Td (A legally binding instrument in the meaning of Article 37\(1\)\(a\) LED has to be concluded by the entity) Tj
0 -13 Td (empowered to enter into obligations with respect to the safeguards provided in the instrument. The) Tj
0 -13 Td (international agreement should thus have the force of law. Such legally binding instrument can be) Tj
0 -13 Td (enforced by the Parties and by data subjects whose personal data processing is governed by the) Tj
0 -13 Td (agreement. The legally binding instrument should contain all relevant rules to allow overcoming any) Tj
0 -13 Td (shortcomings or limitations of the legislation of the third country or international organisation in terms) Tj
0 -13 Td (of data protection by setting a framework of appropriate safeguards that afford an essentially) Tj
0 -13 Td (equivalent level of data protection.) Tj
0 -13 Td (The EDPB considers that the use of a legally binding instrument regulating personal data transfers) Tj
0 -13 Td (between the Parties should, in the absence of an adequacy decision, in principle, take precedence,) Tj
0 -13 Td (over an assessment by the controller according to Article 37\(1\)\(b\) LED as it provides more legal) Tj
0 -13 Td (certainty, transparency, foreseeability, stability, consistency and guarantees on the effective) Tj
0 -13 Td (application of data protection safeguards.) Tj
0 -13 Td (In this context, the EDPB recalls its Statement on international agreements including transfers,) Tj
0 -13 Td (adopted on 13 April 2021, inviting Member States to assess and, where necessary, review their) Tj
0 -13 Td (international agreements that involve international transfers of personal data. The EDPB emphasizes) Tj
0 -13 Td (that consideration should be given to the aim of bringing those agreements in line with the LED) Tj
0 -13 Td (requirements for data transfers, where this is not yet the case, to ensure that the level of protection) Tj
0 -13 Td (of natural persons guaranteed by the LED is not undermined when personal data is transferred outside) Tj
0 -13 Td (the Union.) Tj
0 -13 Td (With respect to Article 37\(1\)\(b\) LED and in light of the above-mentioned greater guarantees offered) Tj
0 -13 Td (by legally binding instruments, competent authorities may rely on such an assessment only when this) Tj
